+## Fork measurement charts
+
+Five charts built from our own measurements. Each chart names the raw files its numbers came from in
+its own footer:
+
+![Optimization steps at 96k](docs/assets/progress-96k.svg)
+
+![Prefill before and after the VRAM fix](docs/assets/windows-vram.svg)
+
+The first shows what each optimization step (super-chunk, flash attention, upload stream) gave at
+96k; the second shows the prefill collapse on an 8 GB card and its removal across the 64k–160k
+windows at `--n-cpu-moe 33`. Every number is traceable to a raw measurement file, which each chart
+footer names; the two optimization steps in the first chart are written up in
+[`docs/research/super-chunk.md`](docs/research/super-chunk.md) and
+[`docs/research/fa-attention.md`](docs/research/fa-attention.md).
+
+![One model, two quants](docs/assets/quant-compare.svg)
+
+![Prefill by model and window](docs/assets/models-windows.svg)
+
+The third chart compares quants on one model (IQ4_XS/Q4_K_M against Q5_K_S at 96k and 128k); the
+fourth places every measured model on the same 64k-160k windows, with gaps left as gaps.
+
+![Strata kernel progress: two baselines, then the working grid](docs/assets/kernel-progress.svg)
+
+The fifth chart is the kernel-progress overview: the fork point `146df3c4` (stock, whose KV stays
+fp32 and therefore stops at 32k with 123.1 pp) and our own 2026-11-01 start (170.5 pp at 64k) as the
+two baselines, then super-chunk N=4, then the working kernel with flash attention across
+64k/80k/96k/128k/160k (1504.0 down to 959.9 pp), with the llama fork as the control line. The
+written-up version, with the table every point came from, is
+[`docs/research/kernel-progress.md`](docs/research/kernel-progress.md).
+
+## Portable kit: both engines, no build step
+
+Both engines of this fork, built for `sm_86`, `sm_89` and `sm_120` and bundled with the CUDA runtime
+they need, are published as an asset of a release:
+[the release page](https://github.com/bahooo22/Strata/releases/tag/kit-2026-11-13) and the direct
+download [gpu-infer-kit-2026-11-13.zip](https://github.com/bahooo22/Strata/releases/download/kit-2026-11-13/gpu-infer-kit-2026-11-13.zip).
+Unpack it, double-click `START.bat`, point it at a `.gguf` file: the kit reads the hardware, compares
+it with our bench, computes the largest window and starts the server. The archive carries no models
+and writes nothing outside its own folder.
+
+Both links were measured on 2026-11-13 with an anonymous request and no token: the release answers
+200 with `draft=false` and `prerelease=false`, and the download returns 852 018 219 bytes starting
+with the zip header `504b0304`. How the kit is built and checked in GitHub Actions, and every
+measurement behind it, is written up in
+[`packaging/kit/README.en.md`](packaging/kit/README.en.md).
